## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design efficient streaming algorithms that trade precision for memory and speed when computing quantiles—a fundamental requirement in real-time monitoring systems.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming quantile estimation using fixed-bin histograms
- Memory-accuracy trade-offs in one-pass algorithms
- Update complexity O(1) per element, query complexity O(K)
- Error analysis and parameter selection (K vs accuracy)
- Comparison with exact solutions using balanced search trees

## Code Example
```javascript
class FixedBinQuantile {
  constructor(M, K) {
    this.M = M;
    this.K = K;
    this.binWidth = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(M / K));
    this.bins = new Array(K).fill(0);
    this.total = 0;
  }

  add(x) {
    const idx = Math.min(this.K - 1, Math.floor(x / this.binWidth));
    this.bins[idx]++;
    this.total++;
  }

  getPercentile(p) {
    const target = Math.ceil(p * this.total);
    let cumulative = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < this.K; i++) {
      cumulative += this.bins[i];
      if (cumulative >= target) {
        return (i + 1) * this.binWidth; // Upper bound of bin
      }
    }
    return this.M;
  }
}
```

## Why This Question Is Asked
Tests the ability to balance space, accuracy, and latency for streaming distinct counts under a sliding window constraint.

## Key Concepts
- Counting Bloom Filter with aging counters
- Sliding window semantics and estimation bias
- Memory-accuracy trade-offs: probabilistic versus exact data structures

## Code Example
```javascript
class SlidingWindowCBF {
  constructor(m, k, windowSize) {
    this.counters = new Array(m).fill(0);
    this.ringBuffer = new Array(windowSize);
    this.head = 0;
    this.k = k;
  }

  hash(id, j) {
    const h = (id * 31 + j * 17) % m;
    return Math.abs(h);
  }

  add(id) {
    for (let j = 0; j < this.k; j++) {
      this.counters[this.hash(id, j)]++;
    }
    this.ringBuffer[this.head] = id;
    this.head = (this.head + 1) % this.ringBuffer.length;
  }

  remove(id) {
    for (let j = 0; j < this.k; j++) {
      this.counters[this.hash(id, j)]--;
    }
  }

  estimateDistinct() {
    return this.counters.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / this.k;
  }
}
```

